# kind | name | source (on-disk LICENSE path for shards; for clib/runtime, an
# SPDX id of licenses-spdx/, or the path of the library's own license file)
#
# Only what the released binary actually embeds: the runtime shard of
# shard.yml (ameba and spectator are development dependencies that never end
# up in it), and the C libraries the stdlib modules crinja requires link.
#
# CONFIRMED on 2026-11-18 against the link line of this very binary, captured
# with `crystal build --static --verbose` in the `crystal` stage of the
# Dockerfile (alpine 3.24.4, Alpine's crystal 1.20.3), the image the linux
# release binaries are built in, on linux/amd64 and on linux/arm64, identical:
#   -lxml2 -lm -lz -llzma -lpcre2-8 -pthread -lgc -ldl  (+ musl, libgcc)
# crinja requires `xml`, hence libxml2, which brings zlib and liblzma along.
# No openssl, no libyaml and no gmp, although the image installs them: nothing
# here requires the stdlib modules that link them.
# Versions and licenses as apk records them in that image: libxml2 2.13.9 MIT,
# zlib 1.4 Zlib, xz 5.8.4, pcre2 10.49 BSD-3-Clause, musl 1.2.6 MIT, gc 8.2.12
# Boehm-GC, libgcc 15.2.0. The darwin binaries link libgc and pcre2 statically,
# from the compiler mise installs; libxml2 and libiconv come from macOS itself
# (`otool -L`: /usr/lib/libxml2.2.dylib, libiconv.2.dylib, libSystem.B.dylib).
# Check the link line again when a stdlib module is added, when crinja moves,
# or when the image moves.
#
# ONE ENTRY CARRIES A JUDGEMENT: apk labels the whole xz suite "GPL-2.0-or-later
# AND 0BSD AND Public-Domain AND LGPL-2.1-or-later", but the GPL parts are the
# command-line tools. The binary links liblzma alone, which is 0BSD.
#
# MIT, BSD-3-Clause and zlib require the copyright notice to be reproduced,
# and their SPDX text only has a blank there: those libraries embed their own
# license file, taken from their sources at the versions above (pcre2, zlib
# and musl are the same files as crystalreleaser's, which links the same
# libraries). liblzma does the same, the SPDX text of 0BSD opening on a blank
# copyright line that upstream's does not have:
#   libxml2  Copyright     gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2    tag v2.13.9
#   liblzma  COPYING.0BSD  github.com/tukaani-project/xz     tag v5.8.4
#   pcre2    LICENCE.md    github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2     tag pcre2-10.49
#   zlib     LICENSE       github.com/madler/zlib            tag v1.4
#   musl     COPYRIGHT     git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl       tag v1.2.6
shard   | crinja   | lib/crinja/LICENSE
clib    | libxml2  | licenses-upstream/libxml2.txt
clib    | zlib     | licenses-upstream/zlib.txt
clib    | liblzma  | licenses-upstream/liblzma.txt
clib    | pcre2    | licenses-upstream/pcre2.txt
clib    | boehm-gc | Boehm-GC
clib    | musl     | licenses-upstream/musl.txt
clib    | libgcc   | GCC-runtime-exception
runtime | crystal  | Apache-2.0
project | envtpl   | LICENSE
